  "content": {
    "id": "p34-q20-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "20",
    "prompt": "How many integers $a$ with $1\\le a\\le 10\\,000$ can be written as a sum of numbers of the form\n$$1,5,5^2,5^3,\\ldots$$\nwhere each power of 5 may be used at most once?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$63$.\n\nEach of six powers is included or omitted; exclude the empty sum.",
      "worked": "Since $5^5=3125$ and $5^6=15\\,625$, only $1,5,5^2,5^3,5^4,5^5$ can be used. Even their total is within the upper bound:\n$$1+5+25+125+625+3125=3906<10\\,000.$$\nEach power has two choices: include it or omit it. Different choices give distinct sums because their base-5 digits are 0 or 1. There are $2^6=64$ choices. The empty choice gives 0, which is excluded by $a\\ge1$.\n$$\\text{Number of integers}=2^6-1=63.$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 60
  },
